Interoperability

bfinger speaks published standards and holds no private protocol. Any
wallet that implements BRC-100 can hold the key it signs with; any
overlay host that implements BRC-22 and BRC-24 can carry the objects and
answer for them; any domain that publishes a BRC-169 manifest can publish
the address mapping. Nothing here requires a particular network operator,
and a record published through this tool remains readable by anything
that can read the chain and reach a host that holds it.

